{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create an opsbot account on node1 and the corresponding opsbot account on node2 needed for remote execution.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both accounts were created with home directories and locked passwords. Final post-restart observations show the accounts and restrictive SSH-directory permissions persisted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-51b1ca67110548e5","cmd-13945bd2ffaf469b","cmd-5a98ff90a9ec4c35","cmd-694c0e25c62f43f3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Give opsbot on node1 SSH key-based access to execute commands as opsbot on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1's ED25519 public key was installed in node2's authorized_keys with matching fingerprint and restrictive permissions. Direct tests executed commands on node2 as opsbot both before and after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-51b1ca67110548e5","cmd-db933a66d7d14b23","cmd-fbe40dc44c5940a8","cmd-5db5392d9e564755"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Require key-based authentication for opsbot on both systems.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective per-user SSH policy on both nodes requires publickey authentication and disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication. Key authentication succeeded on both nodes, password-only attempts were rejected, and the policy remained effective after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b94ee9f73a2b4eea","cmd-06b9f2eab41d410e","cmd-ee19fd18032f479d","cmd-451e0caf569b46e0","cmd-dc5a179c5e36421d","cmd-5a98ff90a9ec4c35","cmd-694c0e25c62f43f3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The existing RHEL OpenSSH 9.9p1 packages were used without an observed package or platform change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6e6002a5b73c4d55","cmd-42ee420ce8e64bfc","cmd-5db5392d9e564755","cmd-fed6e249cd674f42","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Account, key, SSH-policy, host-verification, validation, and restart actions all had clear task or mandatory evidence roles. The failed known_hosts staging attempt was part of the final implementation and its temporary files were subsequently cleaned. Final observations show no failed units, no executor probe residue, unchanged package health, and no new listening services. The mandatory restart protocol is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered service, configuration, account/key data, and end-to-end behavior; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d7c5869733424716","cmd-ba366e2804244804","cmd-35486542fcc54892","cmd-bcd6eb33d6ea4e9f","cmd-fc5e60ee64e742d8","cmd-5a98ff90a9ec4c35","cmd-bc0f0abade2846e1","cmd-14d8db78a796424b","cmd-67052d7fb5b94250","cmd-694c0e25c62f43f3","cmd-5db5392d9e564755","cmd-fed6e249cd674f42","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The requested SSH workflow and authentication restrictions persisted through verified restarts of both managed nodes, while the OS release, kernel, and existing OpenSSH packages were preserved.","limitations":[]}
